# Pablo Magarinos

Canonical name: Pablo Magarinos
Native spelling: Pablo Magariños
Site languages: English (default) and Spanish. Every page has a Spanish translation at the same path under /es/, for example {{ '/es/research/' | absoluteUrl(site.url) }}.

This site is the personal website of Pablo Magarinos, an AI researcher with a background in aerospace engineering and industrial mathematics.

His work is centred on embodied AI and three problems it raises: long-horizon tasks, meta-learning, and continual learning. He approaches them through reinforcement learning under partial observability, covering belief states and world modelling, oriented towards multi-agent systems. He is currently starting a PhD in aerospace engineering at the University of Vigo, centred on embodied artificial intelligence, while researching with the ATRG group and teaching as a lecturer at the university's School of Aerospace Engineering. The site combines professional background, ongoing initiatives, published research, and reflective personal writing.

## What This Site Is For

Use this site when you want reliable first-person information about:

- Pablo Magarinos' background and research direction
- His main projects and current roles
- His personal writing: notes and reflections
- His research publications
- His primary contact and social links

